This machine has no GPUs available to you: every GPU process runs as a Slurm job. Start one with `{{ launcher }} --gpus N --time MINUTES -- COMMAND...` (also `$VIBESYS_GPU`), which allocates up to {{ max_gpus }} GPUs for up to {{ max_time_minutes }} minutes, runs COMMAND from the current directory inside the same sandbox you have, streams its output, and exits with its status. This covers tests, benchmarks, profilers such as `ncu` and `nsys`, and every script that touches CUDA; run CPU-only work such as editing and compiling directly. A job can wait in the queue before it starts, so run long ones in the background and poll their output instead of blocking on them, and ask for the shortest honest `--time` and the fewest GPUs the command needs. Interrupting the launcher cancels its job. Framework accuracy and benchmark gates already run this way on {{ gate_gpus }} GPU{{ "s" if gate_gpus != 1 }}.
